# The EventSourcing hexagon — the ports-and-adapters ring around the Event
# aggregate's synchronous domain core.
#
# One bind : the Event aggregate's persistence port is fulfilled by the AppendLog
# adapter (the bluebook-first Event Log). Append-not-upsert — each Event.Append
# save persists ONE immutable record to this process's private shard, which the
# merge daemon folds into the global ordered event.heki. The domain stays purely
# synchronous (it composes Append, the single writer) ; the shard byte-IO + the
# merge fold are the adapter's kernel leaf, never the domain's concern.
#
# This replaces the imperative record_event_append shard write : the runtime now
# dispatches the bluebook command EventSourcing::Event.Append, and THIS binding
# is what turns that save into a shard append. WHERE the store writes follows the
# heki :default convention (rooted at the realm's data dir), so no .world block
# is needed — the bind alone is the whole wiring.
Hecks.hecksagon "EventSourcing" do
  EventSourcing::Event.persisted_by("AppendLog")
end
